{"time":"2026-10-22T09:23:59.1590358+08:00","level":"INFO","source":{"function":"github.com/nttdata/axet-cli/internal/permission.logHumanDecision","file":"github.com/nttdata/axet-cli/internal/permission/permission.go","line":104},"msg":"User permission decision","event":"permission.decision","source":"human","decision":"grant","tool":"write","action":"write","agent_id":"coder","domain":"edit","pattern":"SPEC.md","description":"Create file C:/Users/xinyee.gan/OneDrive - NTT Ltd/Desktop/Axet Assignment/SPEC.md","path":"C:\\Users\\xinyee.gan\\OneDrive - NTT Ltd\\Desktop\\Axet Assignment","params":"{\"file_path\":\"C:/Users/xinyee.gan/OneDrive - NTT Ltd/Desktop/Axet Assignment/SPEC.md\",\"new_content\":\"# SPEC.md — logscope\\n\\n## Overview\\n**logscope** is a lightweight CLI tool for post-incident log analysis. It streams large log files without loading them entirely into memory, providing quick summaries, timelines, and filtered views to help operations teams investigate incidents fast.\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n### 1. `logscope summary \\u003cfile\\u003e`\\nAnalyzes the entire log file and produces a summary report.\\n\\n**Output includes:**\\n- Count of log entries by level (INFO, WARN, ERROR, DEBUG, TRACE, etc.)\\n- Top 5 most-frequent error messages (by exact text match)\\n- First log entry timestamp\\n- Last log entry timestamp\\n- Total malformed lines encountered\\n\\n**Examples:**\\n```bash\\nlogscope summary app.log\\nlogscope summary app.log --format json\\nlogscope summary app.log --format md  # Writes summary_\\u003ctimestamp\\u003e.md\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. `logscope timeline \\u003cfile\\u003e --bucket \\u003cduration\\u003e`\\nGroups errors by time buckets and displays a text-based bar chart.\\n\\n**Parameters:**\\n- `--bucket` — time interval: `1m`, `5m`, `15m`, `30m`, `1h` (default: `5m`)\\n\\n**Output:**\\n- Time range (start to end of log)\\n- Bucket size\\n- Bar chart where each row is a bucket with error count visualized as `#` symbols (ASCII bar)\\n- Total errors\\n\\n**Examples:**\\n```bash\\nlogscope timeline app.log --bucket 15m\\nlogscope timeline app.log --bucket 1h --format json\\nlogscope timeline app.log --bucket 5m --format md  # Writes timeline_\\u003ctimestamp\\u003e.md\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. `logscope grep \\u003cfile\\u003e [options]`\\nFilters and extracts log lines matching criteria.\\n\\n**Options:**\\n- `--level \\u003cLEVEL\\u003e` — filter by log level (case-insensitive; e.g., ERROR, WARN, INFO)\\n- `--since \\u003cdatetime\\u003e` — only lines with timestamp \\u003e= this value (format: `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`)\\n- `--until \\u003cdatetime\\u003e` — only lines with timestamp \\u003c= this value\\n- `--text \\u003csubstring\\u003e` \ufffd...(truncated)","session_id":"18978d43-1046-40c9-9bd1-7413911bd625","tool_call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PVSVp1S9AihND8CDrzUL3J"}
{"time":"2026-10-22T09:24:24.9725829+08:00","level":"INFO","source":{"function":"github.com/nttdata/axet-cli/internal/permission.logHumanDecision","file":"github.com/nttdata/axet-cli/internal/permission/permission.go","line":104},"msg":"User permission decision","event":"permission.decision","source":"human","decision":"grant","tool":"write","action":"write","agent_id":"coder","domain":"edit","pattern":"PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md","description":"Create file C:/Users/xinyee.gan/OneDrive - NTT Ltd/Desktop/Axet Assignment/PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md","path":"C:\\Users\\xinyee.gan\\OneDrive - NTT Ltd\\Desktop\\Axet Assignment","params":"{\"file_path\":\"C:/Users/xinyee.gan/OneDrive - NTT Ltd/Desktop/Axet Assignment/PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md\",\"new_content\":\"# PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md\\n\\n## logscope — Quick Log Analysis CLI for Operations\\n\\n### Overview\\nThis project delivers **logscope**, a command-line tool built for operations teams to analyze application logs after incidents without dashboards. It streams large files efficiently and provides summaries, timelines, and filtered views.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Language\\n- **Python 3.8+** OR **Node.js 16+**\\n- Choose one; build it in that language.\\n\\n### Core Features\\n1. **summary** — counts by level, top 5 error messages, first/last timestamps\\n2. **timeline** — error count per time bucket with ASCII bar chart\\n3. **grep** — filter by level, timestamp range, or text\\n4. **Formats** — text (default), JSON, Markdown reports\\n5. **Streaming** — handle 100 MB logs without loading fully into memory\\n6. **Robustness** — malformed lines are counted and skipped, never crash\\n\\n### Quality Standards\\n- **Memory efficient:** line-by-line streaming only\\n- **Fast:** 100 MB files process in \\u003c10 seconds\\n- **Robust parsing:** auto-detect log formats (ISO 8601, text, JSON)\\n- **No crashes:** malformed lines counted, reported, skipped\\n- **Exit codes:** 0 = success, 1 = file error, 2 = arg error, 3 = parse error\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n### Code Structure\\n```\\n.\\n├── SPEC.md                          # (Provided) Full specification\\n├── PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md          # This file\\n├── src/                             # (Create; language-specific)\\n│   ├── logscope.py                  # (Python) OR logscope.js (Node.js)\\n│   ├── log_parser.py / parser.js    # Log format detection and parsing\\n│   ├── formatters.py / formatters.js # Output formatters (text, JSON, md)\\n│   └── utils.py / utils.js          # Helpers (time bucketing, arg parsing)\\n├── bin/                             # (Create)\\n│   └── logscope             ...(truncated)","session_id":"18978d43-1046-40c9-9bd1-7413911bd625","tool_call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UoXaobddsAKuX9FcgD8dJe"}
